Statement of Purpose

The laws of most jurisdictions throughout the world automatically confer
exclusive Copyright and Related Rights (defined below) upon the creator
of an original work of authorship and/or a database (each, a "Work").

Certain owners wish to permanently relinquish those rights to a Work for
the purpose of contributing to a commons of creative, cultural and
scientific works ("Commons") that the public can reliably, without fear
of later claims of infringement, build upon, modify, incorporate in other
works, reuse and redistribute as freely as possible in any form
whatsoever and for any purposes, including without limitation commercial
purposes. These owners may contribute their Works to the Commons in
order to advance the goal of a free culture and the production of
creative works for the common good. This License is intended to provide
a clear and standardized way to place a Work in the public domain under
the CC0 license.

For creators who wish to place a Work in the public domain under CC0,
Creative Commons recommends applying CC0 to the Work and prominently
displaying the CC0 mark on the Work, together with a link to the CC0
license text (https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
or a later version) to avoid confusion about the Work's copyright status
and the use of the Work.

1. Copyright and Related Rights.
   A Work made available under CC0 may be protected by a combination of
   copyright and related rights (together, "Copyright and Related
   Rights"). Copyright and Related Rights include, but are not limited
to, the following:

  i. the right to reproduce, adapt, distribute, perform, display,
     communicate, and translate a Work;
 ii. moral rights retained by the original author(s) and/or performer(s);
iii. publicity and privacy rights pertaining to a person's image or
     likeness depicted in a Work;
 iv. rights protecting against unfair competition in regards to a Work,
     subject to the limitations in paragraph 4(a), below;
  v. rights protecting the extraction, dissemination, use and reuse of
     data contained within a Work;
 vi. database rights (such as those arising under Directive 96/9/EC of
     the European Parliament and of the Council of 11 March 1996 on the
     legal protection of databases, and under any national
     implementation thereof, including any amended or successor version
     of such directive); and
vii. other similar, equivalent or corresponding rights throughout the
     world based on applicable law or treaty, and any national
     implementations thereof.

2. Waiver.
   To the greatest extent permitted by, but not in contravention of,
   applicable law, Affirmer hereby overtly, fully, permanently,
   irrevocably and unconditionally waives, abandons, and surrenders each
   of Affirmer's Copyright and Related Rights in the Work for the
   benefit of the public, and to the detriment of Affirmer's heirs and
   successors, and in so doing fully intends that such waiver shall be
   perpetual, irrevocable, and binding under, and subject to, applicable
   law. Affirmer makes this waiver for the benefit of the public
   worldwide. Affirmer understands that this waiver of Copyright and
   Related Rights may have the effect of bringing the Work into the
   public domain in some jurisdictions. Affirmer understands that this
   waiver may narrow or eliminate copyright and related rights in other
   jurisdictions where the waiver is not valid or enforceable. Affirmer
   represents that Affirmer has the right to grant such waiver of
   Copyright and Related Rights, that Affirmer has the authority to do
   so, and that Affirmer's successor(s) in interest will be bound by the
   terms of this waiver.

3. Public Domain Fallback.
   Should any part of the Waiver be unenforceable or invalid for any
   reason, then the Waiver shall be preserved to the maximum extent
   permitted taking into account Affirmer's express Statement of
   Purpose. In addition, to the extent the Waiver is unenforceable or
   invalid for any reason, Affirmer hereby overtly, fully, permanently,
   irrevocably and unconditionally grants, for the benefit of the public,
   and to the detriment of Affirmer's heirs and successors, an
   irrevocable, perpetual, worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free,
   transferable, sublicensable waiver of each of Affirmer's Copyright
   and Related Rights in the Work, to the full extent permitted by, but
   not in contravention of, applicable law. Affirmer makes this grant
   for the benefit of the public worldwide, and in so doing fully
   intends that such grant shall be perpetual, irrevocable, and binding
   under, and subject to, applicable law. Affirmer represents that
   Affirmer has the right to grant such waiver of Copyright and Related
   Rights, that Affirmer has the authority to do so, and that
   Affirmer's successor(s) in interest will be bound by the terms of
   this grant.

